    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for August 20, 2026, centers on capitalizing on favorable park factors and mid-tier pitching matchups. Our strongest play of the day is **Gunnar Henderson** (74.74), who remains an elite start despite facing a high-caliber arm in Gerrit Cole. His score is bolstered significantly by a +16% park adjustment and a +14% boost from the platoon advantage, cementing his role as our primary engine for counting stats. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) also stand out as high-efficiency anchors; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a lucrative +16% park factor and optimal lineup positioning, while **Sam Antonacci** is prioritized as a table-setter at the top of the order, leveraging his speed to maximize our scarcest category.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Nasim Nunez**, who landed on the bench with a score of 36.77. While **Nasim Nunez** provides the elite stolen base upside we prioritize, the brutal matchup against Jacob deGrom\u2014who suppressed the score by 19%\u2014combined with a bottom-of-the-order assignment, rendered him a sub-floor option. We continue to monitor the status of **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, as their absence remains a significant drag on our ceiling. Elsewhere, **Drake Baldwin** (64.69) is a sharp play in the UTIL slot, as his favorable 2-hole placement and high xwOBA against Anthony Kay provide a strong floor in a day where **Heliot Ramos** (64.74) also looks primed to exploit a vulnerable Kyle Bradish.\n\nManagers must remain vigilant as all projected scores are contingent on unconfirmed lineups. We are particularly cautious with **Coby Mayo** (45.87); while he possesses power, his negative platoon split against Gerrit Cole and lower-tier order projection leave him in a marginal zone. If weather reports shift or if **Liam Hicks** (54.32) is pushed down the order by late lineup changes, we may look to shuffle the utility spots. The focus for the Waves today is clear: prioritize the high-efficiency park factors for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos** while navigating the elite arm risk presented by the opposing rotation.",
